    "limitations": [
      "nonCatalogAccount counts accounts absent from bot-stores.json (40 accounts); bictakasaki, bic_kumamoto, bic_itt, bic_urawa exist in the detection catalog (44 stores) and in earlier corpora, so this exclusion is conservative.",
      "Item-noun baseline: a regex over 名刺/アクキー/アクスタ/ステッカー/缶バッジ/ギフトカード/アクリル matches 82 to 83 of 100 positives (by regex variant) and 0 of 100 negatives (precision 1.00; expanded-v2 matches 5 of 100 negatives). No negative mentions a Biccame-musume item, so isEvent is easier than expanded-v2.",
      "Action boundary: posts that end one item and continue another carry the boundary:action tag. They are labelled end when the termination is the main message and update when the post gives substantive new details (condition, place, period) for the continuing item; keep them out of the action main table.",
      "All labels are provisional annotations from the assistant own reading (no model API inference), not human review.",
      "D1 event values (title, category, stores, characters, dates, conditions) are reference-only diagnostics and never gold or model input.",
      "Selected positives reference only manual-or-seed D1 events; the 7 webhook-origin events were excluded by design.",
      "The D1 data is concentrated in 2026 (84 percent of events); older years are scarce, so year coverage is narrower than expanded-v2.",
      "Images and target links were not viewed; image-only information stays unannotated.",
      "Same-family seasonal posts are not independent campaigns; keep cases of one family on the same side of any holdout split."
    ]
